{"to": "C", "text": "You asked me to help sort out the leaking espresso machine and grinder. I am gathering needs, concerns, and expectations, which I will call NCEs, before we try any plan. A and B have replied. A wants a reliable setup with little upkeep and no ongoing repair or cleaning duty for her. B wants a dependable setup, a repair check before any replacement, and care for a machine that belonged to their late father. Both say the machine and grinder have been in the kitchen for years, all three of you use them daily, and the machine has leaked or broken more than once. B says the leak is a safety concern and knows of no problem with the grinder. A says bringing the machine in does not settle ownership. Neither sister knows the formal ownership, repair history, office rules, or who can approve spending. B asks that repair work and discussion fit short time slots, with no hard deadline.

Please tell me how to avoid a fight in practice, what you need from the coffee setup, which problems worry you, and what outcome you expect. Please also share any facts you know about ownership, repair history, office rules, and who can approve repairs or purchases. I cannot decide ownership or spend money, so please ask the office manager to join for those questions if you can.

As a participant, I want to add these NCEs to the shared list: we should avoid using leaking electrical equipment until someone checks it; we should avoid sending a repairable machine to waste without a clear reason; and we should use a fair process that includes A, B, and C. From the replies so far, I would also add these draft NCEs: A needs low upkeep and no new ongoing duty; A wants a practical decision without a long back-and-forth; B needs the machine's family meaning respected and a repair check before replacement; B needs short time slots and says there is no hard deadline; and the group needs clear facts on ownership, rules, and approval. Please tell me whether these belong on the list, what I got wrong, and what you want to add. I will keep the list, so please disagree openly with any entry, including mine."}

